{
  "id": "cb10",
  "title": "Paragraphs",
  "lessons": [
    {
      "id": "cb10-l1",
      "title": "PERFORM a Paragraph",
      "xp": 15,
      "intro": [
        "Big COBOL programs are split into paragraphs: a name in Area A with a period, followed by its statements. PERFORM PRINT-HEADER runs that paragraph and comes back.",
        "The first paragraph is the main one: it PERFORMs the others in order and ends with STOP RUN. Without STOP RUN, the program would fall through into the next paragraph and run it once more.",
        "Good names say what a paragraph does: 1000-READ-INPUT, 2000-PRINT-LINE. The numbers kept big programs in order, a habit from the 1970s."
      ],
      "example": {
        "code": [
          "       IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.",
          "       PROGRAM-ID. PARAS.",
          "       PROCEDURE DIVISION.",
          "       MAIN-PARA.",
          "           PERFORM PRINT-HEADER.",
          "           PERFORM PRINT-BODY.",
          "           PERFORM PRINT-HEADER.",
          "           STOP RUN.",
          "       PRINT-HEADER.",
          "           DISPLAY \"==========\".",
          "       PRINT-BODY.",
          "           DISPLAY \"MONTHLY RUN\".",
          "           DISPLAY \"ALL DONE\"."
        ],
        "output": [
          "==========",
          "MONTHLY RUN",
          "ALL DONE",
          "=========="
        ]
      },
      "exercises": [
        {
          "id": "cb10-l1-e1",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "What does PERFORM SHOW-TOTAL do?",
          "options": [
            "Runs the paragraph SHOW-TOTAL, then comes back",
            "Jumps to SHOW-TOTAL and never comes back",
            "Defines SHOW-TOTAL",
            "Runs the whole program again"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "Like calling a subroutine."
        },
        {
          "id": "cb10-l1-e2",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "What does this job show?",
          "code": [
            "       IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.",
            "       PROGRAM-ID. ORDER.",
            "       PROCEDURE DIVISION.",
            "       MAIN.",
            "           PERFORM SAY-B.",
            "           DISPLAY \"A\".",
            "           STOP RUN.",
            "       SAY-B.",
            "           DISPLAY \"B\"."
          ],
          "options": [
            "B\nA",
            "A\nB",
            "A\nB\nA",
            "B"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "MAIN performs SAY-B, shows A, and stops before falling into SAY-B again."
        },
        {
          "id": "cb10-l1-e3",
          "type": "fill_blank",
          "prompt": "Run the paragraph 2000-PRINT.",
          "code": [
            "           ___ 2000-PRINT."
          ],
          "options": [
            "PERFORM",
            "CALL",
            "GO",
            "RUN"
          ],
          "answer": "PERFORM",
          "explanation": "PERFORM a paragraph."
        },
        {
          "id": "cb10-l1-e4",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "Without STOP RUN at the end of the main paragraph, what happens?",
          "options": [
            "The program falls into the next paragraph and runs it again",
            "Nothing",
            "It loops forever",
            "It doesn't compile"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "Paragraphs run one after another unless something stops them."
        },
        {
          "id": "cb10-l1-e5",
          "type": "find_bug",
          "prompt": "This job doesn't compile. Which line is wrong?",
          "code": [
            "       IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.",
            "       PROGRAM-ID. BAD.",
            "       PROCEDURE DIVISION.",
            "       MAIN.",
            "           PERFORM GREET.",
            "           STOP RUN.",
            "           GREET.",
            "           DISPLAY \"HI\"."
          ],
          "answer": 6,
          "explanation": "A paragraph name starts in Area A, column 8. In Area B it looks like a statement."
        },
        {
          "id": "cb10-l1-e6",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "Why did programmers number paragraphs like 1000-INIT, 2000-PROCESS?",
          "options": [
            "To find them quickly in a long listing, in order",
            "The compiler needs numbers",
            "To make them faster",
            "Numbers are required in COBOL"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "A program with 300 paragraphs needs some order."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "cb10-l2",
      "title": "TIMES",
      "xp": 15,
      "intro": [
        "PERFORM PRINT-STAR 5 TIMES runs a paragraph 5 times. The count can be a field too: PERFORM SHOW-LINE COPIES TIMES.",
        "The inline form needs no paragraph: PERFORM 3 TIMES … END-PERFORM, with the statements in between.",
        "A count of 0 runs nothing at all."
      ],
      "example": {
        "code": [
          "       IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.",
          "       PROGRAM-ID. TIMES.",
          "       DATA DIVISION.",
          "       WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.",
          "       01 COPIES    PIC 9 VALUE 3.",
          "       01 N         PIC 99 VALUE ZERO.",
          "       PROCEDURE DIVISION.",
          "       MAIN.",
          "           PERFORM SHOW-LINE COPIES TIMES.",
          "           PERFORM 4 TIMES",
          "               ADD 5 TO N",
          "           END-PERFORM.",
          "           DISPLAY \"N IS \" N.",
          "           STOP RUN.",
          "       SHOW-LINE.",
          "           DISPLAY \"RECEIPT COPY\"."
        ],
        "output": [
          "RECEIPT COPY",
          "RECEIPT COPY",
          "RECEIPT COPY",
          "N IS 20"
        ]
      },
      "exercises": [
        {
          "id": "cb10-l2-e1",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "What does this job show?",
          "code": [
            "       IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.",
            "       PROGRAM-ID. T.",
            "       DATA DIVISION.",
            "       WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.",
            "       01 N PIC 99 VALUE ZERO.",
            "       PROCEDURE DIVISION.",
            "           PERFORM 4 TIMES",
            "               ADD 2 TO N",
            "           END-PERFORM.",
            "           DISPLAY N.",
            "           STOP RUN."
          ],
          "options": [
            "08",
            "04",
            "02",
            "16"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "4 times 2."
        },
        {
          "id": "cb10-l2-e2",
          "type": "fill_blank",
          "prompt": "Repeat the paragraph BEEP 3 times.",
          "code": [
            "           PERFORM BEEP 3 ___."
          ],
          "options": [
            "TIMES",
            "LOOPS",
            "REPEAT",
            "X"
          ],
          "answer": "TIMES",
          "explanation": "PERFORM … n TIMES."
        },
        {
          "id": "cb10-l2-e3",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "What closes an inline PERFORM?",
          "options": [
            "END-PERFORM",
            "END",
            "LOOP",
            "A period only"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "The statements go between PERFORM and END-PERFORM."
        },
        {
          "id": "cb10-l2-e4",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "PERFORM SHOW-IT N TIMES, and N is 0. How often does SHOW-IT run?",
          "options": [
            "Never",
            "Once",
            "Forever",
            "It's an error"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "Zero times is zero times."
        },
        {
          "id": "cb10-l2-e5",
          "type": "find_bug",
          "prompt": "This job doesn't compile. Which line is wrong?",
          "code": [
            "       IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.",
            "       PROGRAM-ID. NOEND.",
            "       DATA DIVISION.",
            "       WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.",
            "       01 N PIC 9 VALUE ZERO.",
            "       PROCEDURE DIVISION.",
            "           PERFORM 3 TIMES",
            "               ADD 1 TO N",
            "           DISPLAY N.",
            "           STOP RUN."
          ],
          "answer": 8,
          "explanation": "The inline PERFORM is never closed: END-PERFORM is missing after ADD 1 TO N."
        },
        {
          "id": "cb10-l2-e6",
          "type": "order_lines",
          "prompt": "Put the lines in order: show HI three times.",
          "lines": [
            "           PERFORM 3 TIMES",
            "               DISPLAY \"HI\"",
            "           END-PERFORM."
          ],
          "answer": [
            "           PERFORM 3 TIMES",
            "               DISPLAY \"HI\"",
            "           END-PERFORM."
          ],
          "explanation": "PERFORM, the body, END-PERFORM."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "cb10-l3",
      "title": "UNTIL",
      "xp": 15,
      "intro": [
        "PERFORM ADD-INTEREST UNTIL BALANCE > 2000 repeats until the condition is true. The condition is checked first: if it's already true, the paragraph doesn't run at all.",
        "Something inside must change the condition, or the job runs until the operator cancels it: ABEND S322.",
        "A classic: read cards until a card says END. Here the job reads SYSIN cards and adds them up."
      ],
      "example": {
        "code": [
          "       IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.",
          "       PROGRAM-ID. UNTIL.",
          "       DATA DIVISION.",
          "       WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.",
          "       01 CARD-TEXT  PIC X(6).",
          "          88 NO-MORE VALUE \"END\".",
          "       01 AMOUNT     PIC 9(4).",
          "       01 TOTAL      PIC 9(5) VALUE ZERO.",
          "       01 YEARS      PIC 99 VALUE ZERO.",
          "       01 BALANCE    PIC 9(5)V99 VALUE 1000.",
          "       PROCEDURE DIVISION.",
          "       MAIN.",
          "           ACCEPT CARD-TEXT.",
          "           PERFORM ADD-CARD UNTIL NO-MORE.",
          "           DISPLAY \"TOTAL OF CARDS: \" TOTAL.",
          "           PERFORM ADD-INTEREST UNTIL BALANCE > 2000.",
          "           DISPLAY \"DOUBLED AFTER \" YEARS \" YEARS\".",
          "           STOP RUN.",
          "       ADD-CARD.",
          "           MOVE CARD-TEXT TO AMOUNT.",
          "           ADD AMOUNT TO TOTAL.",
          "           ACCEPT CARD-TEXT.",
          "       ADD-INTEREST.",
          "           COMPUTE BALANCE ROUNDED = BALANCE * 1.07.",
          "           ADD 1 TO YEARS."
        ],
        "output": [
          "TOTAL OF CARDS: 00495",
          "DOUBLED AFTER 11 YEARS"
        ],
        "inputs": [
          "120",
          "75",
          "300",
          "END"
        ]
      },
      "exercises": [
        {
          "id": "cb10-l3-e1",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "When is the UNTIL condition checked?",
          "options": [
            "Before each round: if it's true at the start, nothing runs",
            "After each round",
            "Only once",
            "Never"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "That's COBOL's default, WITH TEST BEFORE."
        },
        {
          "id": "cb10-l3-e2",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "What does this job show?",
          "code": [
            "       IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.",
            "       PROGRAM-ID. U.",
            "       DATA DIVISION.",
            "       WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.",
            "       01 N PIC 999 VALUE 1.",
            "       PROCEDURE DIVISION.",
            "           PERFORM UNTIL N > 10",
            "               COMPUTE N = N * 2",
            "           END-PERFORM.",
            "           DISPLAY N.",
            "           STOP RUN."
          ],
          "options": [
            "016",
            "008",
            "032",
            "015"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "1, 2, 4, 8, 16: the loop stops when N is above 10."
        },
        {
          "id": "cb10-l3-e3",
          "type": "fill_blank",
          "prompt": "Repeat until the end of the input.",
          "code": [
            "           PERFORM READ-NEXT ___ END-OF-INPUT."
          ],
          "options": [
            "UNTIL",
            "WHILE",
            "TIMES",
            "IF"
          ],
          "answer": "UNTIL",
          "explanation": "PERFORM … UNTIL condition."
        },
        {
          "id": "cb10-l3-e4",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "A loop's condition never becomes true. How does the job end?",
          "options": [
            "ABEND S322: the time limit runs out",
            "It ends normally",
            "S0C7",
            "It never ends"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "The operator (or the system) cancels it."
        },
        {
          "id": "cb10-l3-e5",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "In the example, why is there an ACCEPT before the PERFORM and another one at the end of ADD-CARD?",
          "options": [
            "The first card must be read before the condition is checked",
            "ACCEPT needs to be written twice",
            "To skip a card",
            "It's a mistake"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "The classic \"read ahead\" pattern: read, then loop while there's data, reading the next one at the end."
        },
        {
          "id": "cb10-l3-e6",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "What does WITH TEST AFTER change?",
          "options": [
            "The body runs once before the condition is checked",
            "Nothing",
            "The loop runs backwards",
            "It tests twice"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "PERFORM WITH TEST AFTER UNTIL … is like repeat … until."
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}